{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012eBU4ZquCVJyCGDLKxcx69","type":"tool_result","content":"290\t    #      that are themselves guarded; leaving the pinner rewritable\n291\t    #      makes the pin decorative (\"pin the pinner\").\n292\t    #\n293\t    # Both are KERNEL tier (no sentinel escape) precisely because a\n294\t    # sentinel that grants an edit to the signer registry could authorize\n295\t    # its own future signer. Deliberately NOT paired with an\n296\t    # \"absence ⇒ fail-closed\" inversion (C10): that would need a\n297\t    # definition of \"expected\" which is itself editable, and would make\n298\t    # DELETING a file the way to choose the posture.\n299\t    \".claude/security/sentinel-signers-registry.yaml\",\n300\t    \".claude/policies/.drift-manifest.json\",\n301\t    # KERNEL-DECOMPOSITION (v1.4.4 train, merge 888e9e6c). These rows\n302\t    # cover the code the v1.4.4 split moved out of seven kernel facades,\n303\t    # the plan-path predicate the train put in place of regexes in two\n304\t    # kernel files, and the modules listed below that kernel code calls.\n305\t    #   - Seven facades moved their code into helper packages. One recursive\n306\t    #     row per package makes that code HARD-DENY again, as it was inside\n307\t    #     the facades in v1.4.2, and a file added there later is HARD-DENY\n308\t    #     too (the federation-dir precedent above).\n309\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/**/*\",  # check_canonical_edit.py\n310\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/agent_spawn/**/*\",  # check_agent_spawn.py\n311\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_policy_parts/**/*\",  # _lib/policy.py\n312\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*\",  # _lib/audit_emit.py\n313\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_log_parts/**/*\",  # audit_log.py\n314\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/**/*\",  # check_bash_safety.py\n315\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_pair_rail_parts/**/*\",  # check_pair_rail.py\n316\t    #   - 