the no-follow ledger read chain (ledger_index.py:55-120) and the gate/main fail-open behavior (runtime.py:108-126).\\n- Condition 5 holds against the code: check_arbitration_kernel.py:309-340 has the 13 new rows, including _pair_rail_parts/**/*, cli_currency.py and plan_paths.py.\\n- Conditions 9 and 10 match the code: part_01.py:553-592 (`compatible`/version_floor_only), part_04.py:510-514 (the command line exits 0 for compatible), and cli_currency.py:11 (CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR = 0.160.0).\\n- _restore_archive.py looks sound:\\n  - It refuses links, hard links, sparse members, absolute paths, `..`, duplicate names, names outside the layout, and the key files under casefold.\\n  - complete_members requires an all-zero end-of-archive block and a clean gzip stream through to the end.\\n  - Extraction uses O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW into a mktemp stage directory (ceo-restore.sh:229-235), and the stage is removed on exit, so a partial write stays inside the stage.\\n- _contamination_inventory.py fails closed through RuleOneInputError (term_scan.py:46-47).\\n- _repin_guard.py only substitutes paths constrained by re-pin-codex.py:246 and :2165.\\n- _subprocess_census.py is Python 3.9-safe; its show_empty pin only applies on 3.13 and later.\\n- architect-bundle-validate.py: the r\\\"\\\"\\\" change leaves __doc__ byte-identical, because the docstring's only backslash escape is \\\\`.\\n- All the Python is standard-library only and compatible with Python 3.9.\\n\\nDECLARED CONDITIONS: none of the conditions reachable from this payload (5, 7, 9, 10) is false against the code. Condition 7 has the caveat in P2-1.\\n\\nP0: none.\\n\\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\\n\\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\\nP2-1 check_pair_rail.py:29-210 vs _lib/_pair_rail_parts/part_02.py:22-314. `_invoke_codex_review` exists twice. The entry point's copy, defined after `_install_parts`, overwrites the rebuilt part_02 copy, so part_02's copy is dead code.\\n- Scenario: a maintainer or adopter follows condition 7 and the CHANGELOG (\\\"re-apply the patch to the module\\\") and patches part_02. The fix silently has no effect at runtime.\\n- Fix: delete one of the two copies. Either drop the entry point's copy, or remove the name from part_02's __all__ and add a comment that the live copy is in the entry point.\\n\\nP2-2 check_precompact_continuity.py:172-175 and _precompact_parts/__init__.py:16. exec of each part's source assigns the part's leading docstring to the namespace's `__doc__`. After install, the hook's `__doc__` is runtime.py's one-line docstring instead of the ADR-153 contract text. audit_log.py:315 and :328 save and restore `__doc__` for exactly this reason.\\n- Fix: save `__doc__` before `_install_precompact_parts(globals())` and restore it afterwards.\\n\\nP2-3 _lib/plan_paths.py:13-23, used at check_plan_edit.py:238-240, 609, 675 and 703. The old regex was search(`\\\\.claude/plans/PLAN-\\\\d{3}-[a-z0-9-]+\\\\.md$`). The new predicate also rejects slugs with a leading, trailing or doubled hyphen, digits other than ASCII 0-9 (the old `\\\\d` accepted them), and a parent that does not end in `/.claude/plans`.\\n- Scenario: a file such as .claude/plans/PLAN-301-foo-.md is still picked up by /ceo-boot (_ceo_boot_parts/state_plan_audit.py:9 globs PLAN-*.md). The lifecycle hook no longer checks its status transitions or required fields.\\n- The same bypass already existed for names with capital letters, so the impact is small.\\n- CHANGELOG.md:332-333 announces only the new FOLLOWUP recognition, not this narrowing.\\n- Fix: declare the narrowing in the CHANGELOG, or have check_plan_edit apply the lifecycle check to any `PLAN-*.md` directly under .claude/plans.\\n\\nP2-4 _lib/_pair_rail_parts/part_01.py:477-486 together with :553-571. When the host's triple is absent from the manifest (the manifest pins only aarch64-apple-darwin), the currency arm runs on the launcher, or on the override path, without resolving or hashing anything.\\n- The result is `compatible` with sha256 empty and path set to the launcher. `_resolve_codex_bin` then runs the launcher.\\n- CHANGELOG.md:191-193 says \\\"the payload's sha256 is still computed and recorded\\\"; that is false on this route.\\n- On the same route, a CEO_PAIR_RAIL_CODEX_BIN override that names a missing file is no longer a fail-closed `mismatch`. It becomes compatible, then FileNotFoundError, then CodexUnavailable, then advisory. The docstring at part_01.py:397-403 still promises \\\"set-but-missing = BLOCK\\\".\\n- Adopters are unaffected, because installs do not receive .claude/governance/ and the pin resolves as infrastructure. The weakening itself is declared in substance by condition 9.\\n- Fix: on the triple-absent route, require an existing regular file before applying the currency arm, and correct the CHANGELOG sentence and the docstring.\\n\\nP2-5 _lib/cli_currency.py:43-60, reached through part_01.py:557-570. `qualified_package_version` returns the closest qualified @openai/codex package.json. `compatible_package_version` keeps walking every ancestor up to `/` and accepts the first one that meets the floor.\\n- Scenario: the closest package says 0.150.0 and an unrelated ancestor package.json named @openai/codex says 0.200.0. The result is status `compatible/version_floor_only` with installed_version 0.150.0, which is below the floor.\\n- Fix: decide compatibility on the same, closest qualified package file, and stop the walk there.\\n\\nP2-6 Docstrings that promise behavior the code no longer has:\\n- part_04.py:498-501: the exit-0 description says \\\"verified (sha matches)\\\" only, but exit 0 now also covers compatible.\\n- part_02.py:63-66: \\\"the artifact that was hashed is the artifact that runs\\\" is not true on the compatible route.\\n- part_01.py:408-418: the status list omits \\\"compatible\\\" and the new installed_version field.\\n- docs/threat-model.md:2601: still names `_PLAN_PATH_RE` in check_plan_edit.py, which no longer exists.\\n- Fix: update the text.\\n\\nP2-7 check_pair_rail.py and check_precompact_continuity.py now fail at import if the _lib subpackages they import are missing, for example after a partial or hand-made upgrade. That is still fail-open, but both rails go silent, leaving only a stderr traceback.\\n- install.sh:1520-1556 copies every top-level _lib entry. scripts/upgrade.sh is withheld from this copy, so I could not check it here.\\n- Fix: none required. Optionally, a /ceo-boot check could confirm that the part packages are present.\",\"decision\":\"GO\",\"sentence\":\"No declared condition reachable from this payload is false and no P0 was found: the pair-rail and precompact entry points keep their globals, patch points and fail-open behavior, the new scripts fail closed where they should, and the remaining items are P2 follow-ups.\"}","structured_output":{"report":"SCOPE OF THIS PAYLOAD (23/32): .claude/hooks/check_pair_rail.py (now an entry point over _lib/_pair_rail_parts), .claude/hooks/check_plan_edit.py (now uses _lib/plan_paths), .claude/hooks/check_precompact_continuity.py (now an entry point over _lib/_precompact_parts), four new scripts (.claude/scripts/_contamination_inventory.py, _repin_guard.py, _restore_archive.py, _subprocess_census.py), and the start of .claude/scripts/architect-bundle-validate.py.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED (no finding)\n- Moved code in check_pair_rail.py (item 4). _pair_rail_parts/__init__.py:14-24 rebuilds every part function on the entry point's own globals (FunctionType(code, namespace, ...)). So:\n  - `__file__` lookups resolve to the entry point. For example, `_emit_codex_review_invoked` computes parents[2] = the repo root, and `_resolve_codex_cli_shape` and `_load_codex_adapter` compute parent = .claude/hooks, as before.\n  - The `global` writes (_CURRENT_REVIEW_ID, _RUBRIC_CATALOGUE_CACHE) land in the entry point's namespace.\n  - Test patch points such as mock.patch.object(check_pair_rail, \"_invoke_codex_review\") still reach _decide.\n  - deepcopy returns the same class o